# 6. Stage 4 — Notes list UI: Legacy ColorNote reference

Use the legacy PWA's unified nine-color system as the visual reference.

Do not reproduce the React PWA's inconsistent seven-color list palette and nine-color editor palette.

### List layout

Use:

- Full-width, vertically stacked, flat note rows.
- No rounded floating cards.
- No large outer margins between cards.
- Thin horizontal separators.
- A saturated vertical color strip at the left edge.
- Soft pastel row background.
- Bold title on the left.
- Modified date aligned on the right.
- Optional subtle checklist indicator.
- No body preview.
- No tag chips in Stage 1.

Approximate native Android sizing:

- Row height: around 64–76dp, allowing growth for a two-line title.
- Left color strip: around 6–8dp.
- Title: around 16–17sp, semibold or bold.
- Date: around 12sp.
- Title: maximum two lines with ellipsis.

Keep the design readable and native. Do not blindly reproduce browser pixel dimensions.

### Untitled note display title

A blank title must never create an empty list row.

Use the following effective display title:

- Text note: explicit title; otherwise first non-empty body line, trimmed; otherwise creation date in `yyyy-MM-dd` format.
- Checklist: explicit title; otherwise first checklist item text; otherwise creation date in `yyyy-MM-dd` format.

This is a display fallback. Do not silently write the fallback into the user's editable title field.

Use the effective display title for alphabetical sorting.

### Unified nine-color palette

Use exactly these nine color identities and maintain consistent mapping across list, editor, color picker, database, sorting, and multi-select.

| Color key | List background | Saturated strip |
|---|---|---|
| White | `#F5F5F0` | `#AAAAAA` |
| Red | `#FCE8E8` | `#E53935` |
| Orange | `#FEF3E2` | `#EF6C00` |
| Yellow | `#FFFDE7` | `#F9A825` |
| Green | `#E8F5E9` | `#2E7D32` |
| Blue | `#E3F2FD` | `#1565C0` |
| Purple | `#F3E5F5` | `#6A1B9A` |
| Black | `#ECEFF1` | `#37474F` |
| Gray | `#F5F5F5` | `#78909C` |

New notes default to **Yellow**.

The editor must use a soft paper tint based on the selected note color, not a harsh neon background.

The header uses the corresponding saturated color and contrast-safe foreground text. Ensure text and icons remain legible for all nine colors, especially Black, Gray, White, Yellow, and Orange.

Do not rely on an incomplete palette lookup that can cause Black or Gray notes to fall back to White.

### Sorting

Support these four options:

1. Modified — default.
2. Created.
3. Alphabetical — case-insensitive, using effective display title.
4. Color — fixed palette order, not alphabetical color names.

Ensure sorting is deterministic and stable when values are equal.

### Search

Implement fast local Notes search.

Search across:

- Note title.
- Text-note body.
- Checklist item text.

Requirements:

- Search only active, non-deleted, non-archived notes.
- Search results must update as the query changes.
- Clear search returns to the normal list.
- Handle blank and whitespace-only queries safely.
